  "preamble": "Devoicing of the voiced postalveolar fricative [ʒ] to [ʃ]. Bulgarian, Macedonian, Czech and Slovak devoice it word-finally as part of general final-obstruent devoicing (Bulgarian нож [nɔʃ], Czech muž [muʃ]). In 16th-century Spanish all voiced sibilants were devoiced, so Old Spanish /ʒ/ merged with /ʃ/ before the merged sound retracted to modern /x/.",
